# llca service rules
#
# These rules name the online services shown in the dashboard's map
# ("Where the agents went"). A service is shown only when the journal proves
# that an agent reached it:
#
#   cli COMMAND NAME      a command line tool that talks to the service
#   mcp SERVER NAME       a connected app (MCP server); SERVER is the part of
#                         the tool name after "mcp__", matched as a prefix
#                         ("codex_apps__sites" matches mcp__codex_apps__sites__…);
#                         the claude_ai_ prefix of Claude's connectors is
#                         optional ("gmail" matches mcp__claude_ai_Gmail__…)
#   domain DOMAIN NAME    a URL on this domain or one of its subdomains, in a
#                         command (curl, git clone…) or a web fetch
#   icon SLUG NAME        the service's logo: SLUG is its name in Simple Icons
#                         (simpleicons.org). Run scripts/brands.py after adding
#                         one; a service without a logo shows its initials.
#
# NAME is the rest of the line. Several rules may give the same NAME: they
# then count as one service. A connected app with no rule is shown under its
# own server name; a domain with no rule is listed under Websites.
# Compiled into the binary: after a change, run `cargo test` and rebuild.

# ---- Command line tools ---------------------------------------------------
cli gcloud Google Cloud
cli gsutil Google Cloud
cli bq Google Cloud
cli aws AWS
cli sam AWS
cli az Azure
cli wrangler Cloudflare
cli cloudflared Cloudflare
cli gh GitHub
cli glab GitLab
cli vercel Vercel
cli netlify Netlify
cli firebase Firebase
cli heroku Heroku
cli flyctl Fly.io
cli fly Fly.io
cli doctl DigitalOcean
cli railway Railway
cli supabase Supabase
cli stripe Stripe
cli eas Expo
cli expo Expo
cli twilio Twilio
cli shopify Shopify
cli sentry-cli Sentry
cli doppler Doppler
cli neonctl Neon
cli turso Turso
cli pscale PlanetScale
cli pulumi Pulumi
cli huggingface-cli Hugging Face
cli hf Hugging Face

